---
description: DQA development and pull request workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read the root AGENTS.md before substantial work.
- Read nested AGENTS.md files for the area being changed.
- Inspect the relevant existing implementation before editing.
- State a small implementation plan before broad changes.
- Keep feature work on a feature branch.
- Never merge a PR unless the user explicitly asks.
- Avoid unrelated refactors.
- Add focused tests for behavior changes.
- Run focused tests before broader regression tests.
- Separate static test success from runtime/deployment validation.
- Report changed files, test results, and remaining risks.
- Prefer ./scripts/deploy.sh once the deployment script exists.
- When a change alters architecture, security boundaries, package contracts, or roadmap sequencing, update the corresponding docs in the same PR.
